# runs/ — pipeline output + the HITL review store. Policy: **git owns the generated CONTENT
# and review state** (JSON / Markdown / txt — small, diffable, and NOT regenerable for
# subagent-authored modules, so remote-session work survives in git), and **ignores only the
# rendered BINARIES** (worksheet PDFs + QA-raster PNGs + sourced asset images — large, churny,
# and rebuildable from the tracked content). Same split as grounding/voices (provenance JSON
# tracked, audio binaries not). The `**` form also matches files directly under runs/.
runs/**/*.pdf
runs/**/*.png
runs/**/*.jpg
runs/**/*.jpeg
runs/**/*.gif
runs/**/*.svg
runs/**/*.webp
runs/**/*.bmp
runs/**/*.tif
runs/**/*.tiff
runs/**/*.wav
runs/**/*.mp3
runs/**/*.flac
runs/**/*.ogg
runs/**/*.m4a
runs/**/*.mp4
# Archives anywhere under runs/ are binary + regenerable.
runs/**/*.zip

# The SRDP Matura corpus (~900 MB) — a large, fully REGENERABLE archive (re-mirror with
# `tools/fetch_matura --all`): raw zips/PDFs + the accessible RTF booklets + the extracted
# JSON. It is not authored content — it stays local/Drive, never git. (Same intent CLAUDE.md
# states; this enforces it — the per-type binary rules above missed the corpus's zip/rtf/json.)
runs/matura/

# Voice reference audio — re-fetchable from VCTK/FLEURS by tools/fetch_*_voices.py
# (the provenance JSON in grounding/voices/ is committed; the binaries are not,
# like the RIS Lehrplan source).
teachersaid/grounding/voices/audio/

# Scratch / prototype output (not engine output) — kept local only, like runs/
output/
tmp/
.claude/worktrees/
